---
// How to delete a Kura Vault account. Play Console requires a page like this that
// works without the app installed; the apps and the Play listing link here.
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../data/site';
---

<Article
  title="Delete your Kura Vault account"
  description="How to delete a Kura Vault account on your own server, a server someone else runs, or one run by Greytimelabs, and what is erased."
  og="delete-account"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Delete your Kura Vault account"
  updated="15 October 2026"
  trail={[{ name: 'Delete your account', path: '/delete-account' }]}
>
  <p>
    Your Kura Vault account lives on the server you signed in to, so that server’s owner is the one who deletes it.
    Pick the case that matches yours.
  </p>

  <h2>On a server run by someone else</h2>
  <p>
    If a family member, friend or your organisation runs the server, ask its owner to delete your account. The owner
    does this in Kura Vault under <strong>Users</strong>, then <strong>Delete</strong> next to your name.
  </p>

  <h2>On a server run by Greytimelabs</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the subject “Delete my account”. Include the
    server address and your username. We may ask you to confirm the request from inside the app before deleting.
    Accounts are deleted within 30 days of a confirmed request, and we will reply once it is done.
  </p>

  <h2>On your own server</h2>
  <p>
    As the owner you can delete any other account under <strong>Users</strong>. To remove everything, including the
    owner account, delete the server’s database and storage bucket.
  </p>

  <h2>What is deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account: username, password hash, keys and sign-in sessions.</li>
    <li>
      Every vault you created, with its albums, photos and videos, for everyone it was shared with. Their encrypted
      files are erased from storage.
    </li>
    <li>Your access to vaults and albums others shared with you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is not deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Photos someone downloaded or saved to their device before the deletion.</li>
    <li>Media you uploaded to a vault someone else created. It stays in that vault for its creator.</li>
    <li>Backups the server’s operator made, until those backups expire.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Only removing it from this device</h2>
  <p>
    To sign out without deleting anything, open <strong>Settings</strong> in the app and sign out of the account. This
    removes its sign-in tokens and any fingerprint or face unlock from the device; the account and its media stay on
    the server. Uninstalling the app does the same.
  </p>
</Article>
